LIGGGHTS (Version LIGGGHTS-PUBLIC 3.8.0, compiled 2026-11-18 09:21:02 by su_estupinan, git commit , build configuration: MPI VTK SQ SMALLBIG, models: HERTZ TANGENTIAL_HISTORY TANGENTIAL_NO_HISTORY COHESION_SJKR COHESION_SJKR2 ROLLING_EPSD2 SURFACE_DEFAULT SURFACE_SUPERQUADRIC)
# sq_04_cube_1cm_edge.in: SUPERQUADRIC reference for the surrogate cube -- Edge contact: 45 deg about x, no spin (matches test_04_cube_1cm_edge.in)
#
# Same setup as the surrogate case (L = 1 cm cube, rho = 1000, Hertz, e = 0.9, mu = 0.2,
# dt = 1e-5, same drop height, orientation and spin), with the cube represented as a
# superquadric: half-axes L/2 and blockiness n1 = n2 = 50 (cube with slightly rounded
# edges/corners). Requires a build with -DENABLE_SQ=ON -DENABLE_MODEL_SURFACE_SUPERQUADRIC=ON.
#
# Expected differences to the surrogate: rounded corners (contact starts a little later,
# softer), inertia from the true rounded shape (slightly below m L^2 / 6), mass rho*V(n).

units           si
atom_style      superquadric
atom_modify     map array
dimension       3
boundary        f f f
newton          off
communicate     single vel yes

region          domain block -0.1 0.1 -0.1 0.1 0.0 0.2 units box
create_box      1 domain
Created orthogonal box = (-0.1 -0.1 0) to (0.1 0.1 0.2)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid

create_atoms    1 single 0.0 0.0 0.1
Created 1 atoms

# Order matters: shape/blockiness/density define volume, mass and inertia;
# quat must precede omega (set omega* converts to angular momentum with quat + inertia).
set             atom * shape 0.005 0.005 0.005 blockiness 50 50 density 1000
  1 settings made for shape
  1 settings made for blockiness
  1 settings made for density
set             atom * quat_direct 0.923879532511287 0.382683432365090 0.000000000000000 0.000000000000000
  1 settings made for quat_direct
set             atom * omegax 0 omegay 0 omegaz 0
  1 settings made for omegax
  1 settings made for omegay
  1 settings made for omegaz

fix             m1 all property/global youngsModulus peratomtype 1.0e9
fix             m2 all property/global poissonsRatio peratomtype 0.25
fix             m3 all property/global coefficientRestitution peratomtypepair 1 0.9
fix             m4 all property/global coefficientFriction peratomtypepair 1 0.2

fix             integrate all nve/superquadric integration_scheme 1
fix             gravity all gravity 9.81 vector 0.0 0.0 -1.0

fix             wall all wall/gran model hertz tangential history surface superquadric primitive type 1 zplane 0.0
WARNING: 
	The contact model you specified is not located in any whitelist.
	Because of this the model will be run in an unoptimized version (increasing runtime by up to 20%).
	In order to optimize this model you have the following options:
		(i)  Run the genAutoExamplesWhitelist.sh script in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder to automatically parse the input script
		(ii) Add the model combination by hand to your style_contact_model_user.whitelist that can be found in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder
		(iii) Use the ENABLE_MODEL_* flag when building with cmake.
	If you perform one of the steps above LIGGGHTS(R) needs to be recompiled to generate the optimized code.

 (/tmp/opencode/sq_src/src/contact_models.h:365)
pair_style      gran model hertz tangential history surface superquadric
WARNING: 
	The contact model you specified is not located in any whitelist.
	Because of this the model will be run in an unoptimized version (increasing runtime by up to 20%).
	In order to optimize this model you have the following options:
		(i)  Run the genAutoExamplesWhitelist.sh script in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder to automatically parse the input script
		(ii) Add the model combination by hand to your style_contact_model_user.whitelist that can be found in your LIGGGHTS(R) source folder
		(iii) Use the ENABLE_MODEL_* flag when building with cmake.
	If you perform one of the steps above LIGGGHTS(R) needs to be recompiled to generate the optimized code.

 (/tmp/opencode/sq_src/src/contact_models.h:365)
pair_coeff      * *

neigh_modify    check no delay 0
timestep        0.00001

compute         ke all ke
compute         erot all erotate/superquadric
variable        epot equal mass(all)*9.81*xcm(all,z)
variable        etot equal c_ke+c_erot+v_epot
variable        zc equal xcm(all,z)
variable        m equal mass(all)
thermo          100
thermo_style    custom step atoms v_zc c_ke c_erot v_epot v_etot
thermo_modify   format float %.10g
